{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok","id":851455,"title":"Charms Enhancing Workings: Is this Ok?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-22T17:04:55-07:00","id":851455,"title":"Charms Enhancing Workings: Is this Ok?","content":"So, I noticed that the Solar Occult Tree includes zero charms, aside from excellencies, that assist in accomplishing a Working. Nothing to shorten intervals or mess with Finesse, Means, or Ambition. And, because of this, I feel like it has to be intentional and not just because of lack of wordcount.<br /> <br /> And, I can see the logic. The way the Working system is set up, you can't get away from adding Time based Means for the top of Solar Ambition even if you have the Means bonuses available to a First Age Solar. Which means that the Salinian Working makes sense and remains a numinous awesome thing that required a team of Solar Sorcerers toiling for years to accomplish. Which is as is should be. Even in Exalted you don't really want people reshaping the fabric of reality on a whim. <br /> <br /> But..... I can't help but notice that Craft, which also generates permanent items, can get up to some crazy, crazy things with the set of existing Solar Craft charms. Including things like &quot;Here, you've been working so hard, have a daiklave!&quot; basically. Or &quot;Ha! You didn't actually kill me! This body is simply a tele-operated robot clone! With a Self-Destruct Mechanism!&quot; *BOOM* <br /> <br /> So, I'm not entirely sure that easier access to Workings would necessarily be that much more problematic than the kind of things you can do with Supernal Craft. And, even if we do want to keep Solar level Workings rare and special, I still kinda wonder if warding a town against fleas should really need to take an entire week, minimum. There might be some things we can do where making Terrestrial or Celestial Workings gets a bit easier, without creating a charm that lets you perform the Salinian Working as a simple action.<br /> <br /> So what do you guys think? Are charms that mess with Workings bad design space? Would a Spell be a better idea?<br /> <br /> Are charms that enhance spells bad ideas too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:16:11-07:00","id":851461,"title":"","content":"Aren't there Lore Charms that affect Workings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:53:44-07:00","id":851475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851461#post851461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't there Lore Charms that affect Workings?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the leak Heaven Turning Calculations did, in the backer PDF, not so, I was pointed to that in another thread. The only charms that affect Working Rolls are (besides Occult Excellency) Supernal Control Method (free full excellency), Ancient Tome Understanding (Essence/2 round down, regular charm successes) and Fate-Shifting Solar Arete (Pick 1, or 2 with Ess 4 repurchase, numbers from 2 to 5 to count as 10s for any action). Of the 3 FSSA is supposedly being amended in some way.<br /> <br /> The consensus seems to be that Workings are balanced around not having Charms. You have the Ambition, Finesse and Means to play with. Including Charms may make those irrelevant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:39:22-07:00","id":851555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok#post851455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm not entirely sure that easier access to Workings would necessarily be that much more problematic than the kind of things you can do with Supernal Craft. And, even if we do want to keep Solar level Workings rare and special, I still kinda wonder if warding a town against fleas should really need to take an entire week, minimum. There might be some things we can do where making Terrestrial or Celestial Workings gets a bit easier, without creating a charm that lets you perform the Salinian Working as a simple action.<br /> <br /> So what do you guys think? Are charms that mess with Workings bad design space? Would a Spell be a better idea?<br /> <br /> Are charms that enhance spells bad ideas too?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we'll probably see a thing or two like this, but I would hesitate to just throw stuff in because it looks like things you can do in Craft. Craft very much gives me the impression that the baseline constraints were designed to allow charms to remove them, key to lock. Workings are probably calibrated under the assumption that those things do not exist (perhaps because they are their own XP tax), so adding them risks making it too easy.<br /> <br /> The other thing that I think needs to be accounted for is that with sorcerous workings, while there's a work-time attached, you are more or less assumed to have the ability to get right to work immediately, and any extra prep you put in manifests as Means. In Crafting, this isn't the case -- the amount of prep needed is entirely fiat-based and implicitly significant in many cases, which means that it's easy to put the brakes on crafting if your speed gets too out of hand. (On the other hand, sorcery has the XP sink, so that might have the same effect?)<br /> <br /> All that being said, I totally think there's room for working-enhancing charms, and I do expect we'll see some eventually. But I would hesitate to use the Craft charms as a model, because I expect they'll operate on a rather smaller scale and not be direct force multipliers in the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-22-2016, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:41:12-07:00","id":851556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851475#post851475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the leak Heaven Turning Calculations did, in the backer PDF, not so, I was pointed to that in another thread. The only charms that affect Working Rolls are (besides Occult Excellency) Supernal Control Method (free full excellency), Ancient Tome Understanding (Essence/2 round down, regular charm successes) and Fate-Shifting Solar Arete (Pick 1, or 2 with Ess 4 repurchase, numbers from 2 to 5 to count as 10s for any action). Of the 3 FSSA is supposedly being amended in some way.<br /> <br /> The consensus seems to be that Workings are balanced around not having Charms. You have the Ambition, Finesse and Means to play with. Including Charms may make those irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, ignoring FSSA for the moment, you'll note that all the other charms simply add more charm dice (or the equivalent) to the roll, and thus are effectively equivalent to an excellency in effect, if not in mote cost. <br /> <br /> Thinking on it further, while Spells that enhance Workings seems kinda thematic, it also means that Workings would have to be rebalanced around assuming everyone had that Spell, which pretty much becomes a tax on being good at Workings.<br /> <br /> A few charms, on the other hand, seems like they could be introduced that wouldn't end up tossing the whole system out the window, just tipping the Solar end of the scale a bit.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm thinking of one or two charms which branch off the Sorcery access charms that give you boosts to the circle of Workings under the one you just got access to. So, you learn Celestial Circle Sorcery, now you can get a couple of charms which boost your ability to do Terrestrial Workings. This way, at least, no-one is introducing any charms which make Solar level workings easier.<br /> <br /> As for what the charms might do, well, here are some possible ideas (and note that these would be limited to certain circles of Working):<ul><li>Double 9s on Workings and/or Shaping Rolls.</li> <li>If you roll a set of 666, you get 3 non charm successes on a Working and/or Shaping Roll.</li> <li>Each pair of a 10 and an 8 counts as 4 successes on a Working and/or Shaping Roll. (Possibly this fits better as a Sid charm).</li> <li>Lower the Interval of your Working.</li> <li>Subtract 5 from the Ambition Number of your Working.</li> <li>Turn a Botch into 5 successes.*</li> <li>Treat a Working as if you had the proper Equipment, raising Means by 1.</li> </ul><br /> I suspect that messing with Finesse is probably gonna be broken. And, hmmm,,, Of the things I came up with, I think that what I want the most is a way to reduce the time on some Workings, which might well be a warning flag. I think that a charm which lets you count as though you had a particular type of Means when you don't might be the least disruptive to balance, especially if it was limited to certain types of Workings. <br /> <br /> I think the effect I like the most is a charm that turns a Botch into some number of successes, because I realized that it could be fluffed as the person having a big insight into the Working that causes them to reevaluate the Working. Maybe it doesn't actually add successes, it just lets the Player or Character dictate the change to the project as a result of the Botch, turning it from a bug into a feature. Yeah, I think that's a charm I could introduce without breaking the system too horribly and injecting a bit of fun into the game. Especially if it was 1 use per Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:57:52-07:00","id":851559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851555#post851555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we'll probably see a thing or two like this, but I would hesitate to just throw stuff in because it looks like things you can do in Craft. Craft very much gives me the impression that the baseline constraints were designed to allow charms to remove them, key to lock. Workings are probably calibrated under the assumption that those things do not exist (perhaps because they are their own XP tax), so adding them risks making it too easy.<br /> <br /> The other thing you need to account for is that the baseline for sorcerous workings is that while there's a work-time attached, you are more or less assumed to have the ability to get right to work immediately, and any extra prep you put in manifests as Means. In Crafting, this isn't the case -- the amount of prep needed is entirely fiat-based and implicitly significant in many cases, which means that it's easy to put the brakes on crafting if your speed gets too out of hand. (On the other hand, sorcery has the XP sink, so that might have the same effect?)<br /> <br /> All that being said, I totally think there's room for working-enhancing charms, and I do expect we'll see some eventually. But I would hesitate to use the Craft charms as a model, because I expect they'll operate on a rather smaller scale and not be direct force multipliers in the same way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The base Craft system seems designed around the idea that, unless you have Craft charms, or another source of awesome, you're almost certainly not going to be able to build anything supernatural. Which lets you fine tune just how good each type of Exalt is at Crafting. Solars are awesome, so they get to pull out all the stops on Crafting. DBs, I suspect, will probably get to be pretty awesome at mundane crafting, including a few tricks that Solars probably don't get (I hope), but will be much more limited in the Artifact/Manse Crafting arena.<br /> <br /> The only reason I brought up Craft in the beginning is because, if you have a dedicated Artificer on your team, they can make some crazy crazy disruptions to the status quo. Workings have the same potential to disrupt the setting, but Workings seem to be more hamstrung for Solars than Crafting Artifacts. On the other hand, buying all the Craft charms in the Core is a ~400xp to ~500xp investment, while getting good at Workings costs between 24xp and 30xp, so I guess I can see why one has the limiters removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:58:14-07:00","id":851560,"title":"","content":"The thing about Workings is...for the price of buying charms to boost your workings, you could just get better Attributes and Abilities and dump an excellency in. If you're only boosting the ability to do Terrestrial and Celestial, you're boosting the easy, short ones anyway. 10m a roll when you're rolling once per week is not much of a price to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:59:48-07:00","id":851562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851556#post851556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]If you roll a set of 666, you get 3 non charm successes on a Working and/or Shaping Roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please no, Material Exegesis Prana was cringy enough. If you must make it a number, make it a 1, a 10 and an 8 (108) or at least something vaguely relevant to the setting. I don't need <i>another</i> christian boogyman number in my Wuxia fantasy game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 03-23-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T21:11:47-07:00","id":851573,"title":"","content":"I think the major difference between Craft and Workings is that, by design, it's mathematically impossible to reach the highest tiers of crafting unless you have Solar Charms. It makes it so everyone uses the same rules, but Legendary projects are the exclusive purview of Solars <i>without</i> forcing them to buy a speedbump charm just so they can make N/A Artifacts. <br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings don't really have that. So long as a sorcerer is dedicated enough, they can make anything up to an Ambition 2 Solar Working. <br /> <br /> Aside from granting more dice, I don't see what else Charms could add to Workings. Maybe a grab-bag Charm like Master Horseman's Techniques that can make minor enhancements to Means?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T21:25:23-07:00","id":851579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851556#post851556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the effect I like the most is a charm that turns a Botch into some number of successes, because I realized that it could be fluffed as the person having a big insight into the Working that causes them to reevaluate the Working. Maybe it doesn't actually add successes, it just lets the Player or Character dictate the change to the project as a result of the Botch, turning it from a bug into a feature. Yeah, I think that's a charm I could introduce without breaking the system too horribly and injecting a bit of fun into the game. Especially if it was 1 use per Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rad as hell, I agree. I would probably require that it leave the flaw in, but leverage it somehow. A few other possibilities I can think of that seem more flavourful than straight force-multipliers but still cool enough to be Charms:<ul><li>Choose three narrow, specific specializations in the vein of &quot;spirits&quot;, &quot;protection&quot;, &quot;orichalcum&quot;, or &quot;hands&quot;. Any working of finesse 3-5 that is built around two or more of these specializations is attempted at -1 difficulty, reflecting the sorcerer's proficiency with effects of that type.</li> <li>If the sorcerer has a relevant Defining Tie, this counts as a Means, so long as they maintain that Tie for the duration of the Working and, during that time, do not resist persuasion that targets it during Decision Points. (Non-stacking.)</li> <li>If you lower a working's Finesse in order to complete it, the change is retroactive, granting the appropriate number of extra successes for every past roll. In this case, the elements of the working decided by the ST (both from lowered Finesse and added botches) reflect subconscious manifestations of the sorcerer's psyche, past lives, or Great Curse. Using this Charm triggers a three-die Limit check.</li> <li>After performing a sorcerous working roll, the sorcerer may reduce the terminus by one in order to reroll all failed dice. (Only possible if not yet at the terminus.)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-23-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T00:39:04-07:00","id":851613,"title":"","content":"It's a neat idea, but how often are you gonna botch? You have every incentive to use a full excellency and a point of willpower.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/818771-ex3-homebrew-so-i-heard-you-like-sorcery\">Anyway, check this out.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:26:20-07:00","id":852505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851562#post851562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please no, Material Exegesis Prana was cringy enough. If you must make it a number, make it a 1, a 10 and an 8 (108) or at least something vaguely relevant to the setting. I don't need <i>another</i> christian boogyman number in my Wuxia fantasy game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one right after that was a pair of a 10 and an 8, so I went there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:12:20-07:00","id":852557,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that having relevant charms, spells and other resources already boosts the means of a project. So we do already have that tie in, and it's one that encourages you to make workings in alignment with what you already do/have access to.<br /> <br /> The headache(as others have already pointed out) is that for solars it's trivial to just Throw an Excellency at it, as this is a longer-term project so generally motes are not an issue, so while charms that give you automatic successes or more dice cheaply might be a thing you can do, it doesn't add a lot to the game to do so. On the other hand, you want to be careful about non-charm dice or successes, as suddenly that makes very high level projects a lot easier/more probable to do.<br /> <br /> So that really only leaves the ground of decreasing the XP costs, decreasing the time they take to make or maybe making it easier to juggle several at once. Which is good grounds, just not as much as we might like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:52:38-07:00","id":852735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851562#post851562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please no, Material Exegesis Prana was cringy enough. If you must make it a number, make it a 1, a 10 and an 8 (108) or at least something vaguely relevant to the setting. I don't need <i>another</i> christian boogyman number in my Wuxia fantasy game.</div> </div> </div> </div>666 is an incredibly lucky number in Chinese numerology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:37:57-07:00","id":852790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=852505#post852505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one right after that was a pair of a 10 and an 8, so I went there too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I must have missed that. Your version is better than mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=852735#post852735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">666 is an incredibly lucky number in Chinese numerology.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick google search shows that it is indeed, that's pretty neat. Still think it's a bad idea, as it's a little obscure and 666 has a very specific meaning to western culture, which I think is the majority of Exalted's player base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:00:53-07:00","id":852824,"title":"","content":"Sure, I thought of the Christian thing before the Chinese thing myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:57:14-07:00","id":853094,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind that the number 666's link to the number of the Beast is itself a result of shitty translation. It could very well have been 6<i>1</i>6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:09:50-07:00","id":853101,"title":"","content":"True, but to be fair only nerds and losers like us who spend time in make believe land would know that, whereas the majority of Exalted's target audience would lack that tidbit of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:13:28-07:00","id":853104,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the Christian reference was the intended one. Bear in mind, this Charm is mostly useful to demon-summoners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:45:26-07:00","id":853119,"title":"","content":"Hope not, it would be very weird to have such a blatantly christian reference in an otherwise wholly wuxia/pulp fantasy game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:32:08-07:00","id":853166,"title":"","content":"Well, Exalted has lots of <i>Old </i>Testament references, but I can't imagine it would be the only explicitly Christian influence in there. It's a very syncretic.game, on the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:59:48-07:00","id":853633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=852557#post852557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that having relevant charms, spells and other resources already boosts the means of a project. So we do already have that tie in, and it's one that encourages you to make workings in alignment with what you already do/have access to.<br /> <br /> The headache(as others have already pointed out) is that for solars it's trivial to just Throw an Excellency at it, as this is a longer-term project so generally motes are not an issue, so while charms that give you automatic successes or more dice cheaply might be a thing you can do, it doesn't add a lot to the game to do so. On the other hand, you want to be careful about non-charm dice or successes, as suddenly that makes very high level projects a lot easier/more probable to do.<br /> <br /> So that really only leaves the ground of decreasing the XP costs, decreasing the time they take to make or maybe making it easier to juggle several at once. Which is good grounds, just not as much as we might like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say the only grounds. I like that idea I had about letting the player get to choose the result of one botch, since it could change the way someone tries to run one of these. Especially if that charm applies to all workings, instead of just a particular circle like I've been thinking.<br /> <br /> Another spot to go that would be useful, but wouldn't necessarily change the math, would be a charm which lets you retain the benefit of one particular set of Means if you would otherwise lose access to them. <br /> <br /> Or...hmmm. Ok this might be tricky to balance, but what about a charm that let you trade some number of extra rolls from Means in exchange for a reduction in either Ambition or Finesse? Or some additional benefit, like being able to work on a second Working at once?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T16:52:44-07:00","id":853745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/851455-charms-enhancing-workings-is-this-ok?p=851475#post851475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the leak Heaven Turning Calculations did, in the backer PDF, not so, I was pointed to that in another thread. The only charms that affect Working Rolls are (besides Occult Excellency) Supernal Control Method (free full excellency), Ancient Tome Understanding (Essence/2 round down, regular charm successes) and Fate-Shifting Solar Arete (Pick 1, or 2 with Ess 4 repurchase, numbers from 2 to 5 to count as 10s for any action). Of the 3 FSSA is supposedly being amended in some way.<br /> <br /> The consensus seems to be that Workings are balanced around not having Charms. You have the Ambition, Finesse and Means to play with. Including Charms may make those irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>This this this this this. This has been a particular hobbyhorse of mine. The whole idea of Workings is that they've already built in a system for regulating which splats should be able to achieve which effects at which essence at what cost in time and infrastructure. That's the point of the Circle / Ambition / Means system. It's not supposed to be possible to get ahead of that framework. Any kind of math-boosting (i.e. double Xs or non-charm dice) breaks that.<br /> <br /> I get that this is counterintuitive, because everywhere else in Exalted their system does none of this balancing, and splat-specific charms are what regulate it. But they designed Workings differently, and math-boosting charms are not supposed to play any role.<br /> <br /> If you want to get better at Workings, get a powerful demesne, or assemble a sorcerous laboratory, or secure the assistance of an academy of sorcerers, etc. Those are all in the Means list, and represent durable, repeatable enhancements to your ability to succeed at a working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 03-26-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:13:52-07:00","id":855206,"title":"","content":"What do people think of this?<br /> <br /> Flawed Trait Epiphany <br /> Cost: NA ; Mins: Occult 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent <br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: NA<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> When the Solar is in danger of making a fatal error, such is their genius that, not only will they see it, but it will inspire them to greatness. If the Solar botches a Working roll, they may choose the effect of the botch, with the ST's input, instead of the ST choosing it on their own. This charm may only be used once per Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:13:56-07:00","id":855282,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't pay 8 xp for that even if I were a mortal sorcerer, to be honest, because It's a small benefit that applies only in a rare situation. This is the problem with effects that trigger only on working botches: if they're strong, botching seems counterintuitively good, but if they're weak, the rarity of working botches makes them too modest to pay XP for.<br /> <br /> How about something like this:<br /> Cost: --. Once per working, you can use Instant-duration powers or spend WP to enhance a working roll <i>after </i>making the roll, retroactively adding dice or successes or what have you (needs rewrite obv). The usual spending and bonus limits still apply to the roll as a whole.<br /> <br /> Botches are only going to happen in situations where you're phoning in the attempt, so this would give you a way to prevent a botch while also having a broader functionality in cases where you're not going completely all-out. However, it doesn't really warp the curve since it doesn't raise the ceiling on your performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:02:26-07:00","id":855350,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you could easily go an entire campaign without using that Charm once. And if you did use it, it wouldn't really be that big a deal.<br /> <br /> If I were you I'd fold it into a Charm offering a more powerful effect. Like reduced penalties for reaching beyond your circle of sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:49:45-07:00","id":855390,"title":"","content":"Had an idea that seems appropriate for this thread.<br /> <br /> Glory Born of Madness<br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Occult 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive <br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> The greatest workings of the Solar god-kings were tinged with fatal hubris. When rolling for a Working, the sorcerer may use this Charm to add Essence non-Charm successes to the roll. However, doing so alters the results of the Working as though the roll was botched. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T19:23:00-07:00","id":1524376,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread in 2023, I can see half the problem is settingfluff...<br /> <br /> In 1e and 2e, sorcery was only discovered after the defeat of the primordials. The exalted host was never designed to be good at sorcery, that was the purview of the primordials. That is why there are so few charms affecting sorcery and sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> While I haven't read all the splits in detail, I suspect this is the same.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> You can also consider that one can easily just make custom charms based on what you see in other charm trees. Lots of charms have things like &quot;double 7's and reroll all 1's.&quot; pay some motes and willpower or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 11-13-2023, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}